    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1006">

                <pb facs="0762" n="646" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg646"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 703.3212/18.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul General Hanna to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monterey</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 15, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Consul Silliman, from Teoloyucan, August 13, asks me to telegraph following:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>To the Brazilian Minister solely is due the preparation of the document
                            which was signed this afternoon terminating the civil war in Mexico.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman</hi>.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>It is also proper for the Department to know how great a source of help and
                    strength the Brazilian Minister has been to our Consuls in Mexico.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
